# Neural CSSR Experiments Log

Date: <fill with run date>

## Scope
- Validate Neural CSSR against the transCSSR reference using empirical counts.
- Inject neural probabilities into the reference (unchanged mechanics) and tune to avoid oversplitting.
- Add diagnostics to compare neural vs empirical probabilities (WMSE, CSV dump).

## Files of Interest
- Runner (single-file Neural CSSR): `neural_cssr_state_averaging.py`
- Reference CSSR (unchanged): `transCSSR/transCSSR.py`
- Neural → transCSSR injector: `transcssr_neural_runner.py`

## Baseline (Empirical parity)
Golden Mean (empirical, Neural CSSR runner)
```bash
uv run python /home/matteo/NeuralCSSR/neural_cssr_state_averaging.py \
  --data /home/matteo/NeuralCSSR/experiments/datasets/golden_mean/golden_mean.dat \
  --backend empirical --L_max 4 --alpha 0.001 --test_method chi2 \
  --output_json /home/matteo/NeuralCSSR/neural_cssr_result_gm_empirical.json
```
Outcome: 2 states (matches reference Golden Mean).

Even Process (empirical, reference dataset)
```bash
uv run python /home/matteo/NeuralCSSR/neural_cssr_state_averaging.py \
  --data /home/matteo/NeuralCSSR/transCSSR/data/even_process_10k.dat \
  --backend empirical --L_max 10 --alpha 0.001 --test_method chi2 \
  --output_json /home/matteo/NeuralCSSR/neural_cssr_result_even_empirical_10k.json
```
Outcome: aligned after parity fixes (epsilon mapping, determinization, transient removal, history pruning).

## Neural CSSR (state_averaging.py)
Golden Mean (neural, tuned)
```bash
uv run python /home/matteo/NeuralCSSR/neural_cssr_state_averaging.py \
  --data /home/matteo/NeuralCSSR/experiments/datasets/golden_mean/golden_mean.dat \
  --model_ckpt /home/matteo/NeuralCSSR/experiments/ebm/checkpoints/golden_mean_ar.pt \
  --backend neural --L_max 4 --alpha 0.001 --test_method chi2 --device cuda \
  --pseudo_count_scale 20 --min_count 5 \
  --output_json /home/matteo/NeuralCSSR/neural_cssr_result_gm_neural_ps20_a1e3.json
```
Notes:
- Capped eff_ext = min(count, pseudo_count_scale) in tests to reduce spurious splits.
- Using chi2 (alpha=1e-3) and min_count=5 yielded stable 2-state results on GM.

WMSE diagnostic (GM)
```bash
uv run python /home/matteo/NeuralCSSR/neural_cssr_state_averaging.py \
  --data /home/matteo/NeuralCSSR/experiments/datasets/golden_mean/golden_mean.dat \
  --model_ckpt /home/matteo/NeuralCSSR/experiments/ebm/checkpoints/golden_mean_ar.pt \
  --backend neural --L_max 4 --alpha 0.001 --test_method chi2 --device cuda \
  --dump_prob_diff /home/matteo/NeuralCSSR/prob_diffs_gm.csv --diff_min_count 5 \
  --output_json /home/matteo/NeuralCSSR/neural_cssr_result_gm_neural_tuned.json
```
Outcome: Weighted MSE (neural vs empirical) ≈ 0.013; small biases can still trigger splits without tuning.

## Neural injection into reference (transcssr_neural_runner.py)
Defaults set for stable neural results:
- `pseudo_count_scale=50`, `--cap_marginal_counts` (on), `--mix_empirical=0.3` (Platt optional).

Golden Mean (neural-injected)
```bash
uv run python /home/matteo/NeuralCSSR/transcssr_neural_runner.py \
  --data /home/matteo/NeuralCSSR/experiments/datasets/golden_mean/golden_mean.dat \
  --model_ckpt /home/matteo/NeuralCSSR/experiments/ebm/checkpoints/golden_mean_ar.pt \
  --backend neural --L_max 4 --alpha 0.001 --test_method chi2 --device cuda \
  --output_json /home/matteo/NeuralCSSR/transcssr_neural_result_gm_tuned.json
```
Outcome: Matches empirical topology with tuned defaults.

Even Process (neural-injected, L=6)
```bash
uv run python /home/matteo/NeuralCSSR/transcssr_neural_runner.py \
  --data /home/matteo/NeuralCSSR/transCSSR/data/even_process_10k.dat \
  --model_ckpt /home/matteo/NeuralCSSR/experiments/ebm/checkpoints/even_process_ar_long.pt \
  --backend neural --L_max 6 --alpha 0.001 --test_method chi2 --device cuda \
  --output_json /home/matteo/NeuralCSSR/transcssr_neural_result_even_l6.json
```
Diagnostics (prob diffs + WMSE)
```bash
uv run python /home/matteo/NeuralCSSR/transcssr_neural_runner.py \
  --data /home/matteo/NeuralCSSR/transCSSR/data/even_process_10k.dat \
  --model_ckpt /home/matteo/NeuralCSSR/experiments/ebm/checkpoints/even_process_ar_long.pt \
  --backend neural --L_max 6 --alpha 0.001 --test_method chi2 --device cuda \
  --dump_prob_diff /home/matteo/NeuralCSSR/transcssr_prob_diffs_even_l6.csv \
  --output_json /home/matteo/NeuralCSSR/transcssr_neural_result_even_l6.json
```

Empirical (reference parity check)
```bash
uv run python /home/matteo/NeuralCSSR/transcssr_neural_runner.py \
  --data /home/matteo/NeuralCSSR/transCSSR/data/even_process_10k.dat \
  --backend empirical --L_max 10 --alpha 0.001 --test_method chi2 \
  --output_json /home/matteo/NeuralCSSR/transcssr_empirical_result_even.json
``;

## Key Implementation Notes
- Empirical parity fixes in `neural_cssr_state_averaging.py`:
  - epsilon-only mapping (prefer longer histories), determinization by conflict split, transient removal (largest SCC), prune histories < L_max−1.
  - Empirical backend compares raw counts (chi2/G), moves counts on splits, and recomputes morphs from counts.
- Neural tests cap per-history effective counts and allow chi2 alpha tuning to balance power.
- transCSSR injector preserves reference mechanics; only replaces future counts via neural probabilities (with optional calibration and mixing).

## Suggested Defaults
- `test_method=chi2`, `alpha=0.001`.
- Neural: `pseudo_count_scale∈[20,50]`, `cap_marginal_counts`, `mix_empirical∈[0.2,0.5]`, `platt_fit` optional.

## Next Steps
- Add optional intermediate-state tracing to pinpoint first divergence vs transCSSR on Even Process.
- Export DOT from Neural CSSR for visual parity.

